/*
 * TestArm64Semantics.cpp
 *
 * Tests of the ARM lifter (ArmSemantics.h): the A64 base instructions run by
 * the interpreter against the values the Arm ARM defines (the rows of
 * tests/arm/Arm64SemanticRows.inc, generated by tests/arm/tools/
 * gen_semantic_rows.py from an independent model of the pseudocode), the
 * classification, and the AArch32 rules of the lifter (the condition wraps the
 * instruction, pc reads as the address + 8 / + 4, the writes of pc interwork)
 * on hand built instructions.
 *
 * The differential tests against Unicorn and the M4 (tests/arm/semantics)
 * cover the instructions those processors implement; these rows cover the
 * ones neither does (CSSC, LSUI, HBC, LS64, the writeback forms of LRCPC3),
 * and pin the others.
 *
 * Author: Elad Raz <e@eladraz.com>
 */
